An arm leaves the Irq naming the core that armed it before, or the first,
so once a tick looks at the lines that core's timer wakes for the deadline and the arming core's does not;
a timer line wakes the core that armed it.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: armed timer line comes due before the timer wakes for it

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -43,7 +43,6 @@ void irq_set_bits(struct irq *irq, uint32_t bits)
      */
     if (line_is_timer(irq->line) && bits != 0) {
         struct core *core = core_self();
-        irq->core = (uint8_t)core_index();
         if (tick_before(irq->deadline, core->nearest_deadline)) {
             core->nearest_deadline = irq->deadline;
             core->wake_stale = true;
